$\mathbf{q}$, is determined by what is called the bidirectional reflection distribution function (BRDF), $F$, of the surface. If the surface normal is $\mathbf{n}$, then outgoing power is some function, $F$, of the surface normal, the incoming and outgoing ray directions, the wavelength, and the incoming light power:
$$\ell_{\texttt{out}} = F \left( \ell_{\texttt{in}}, \mathbf{n}, \lambda, \mathbf{p}, \mathbf{q} \right)
$$ {#eq-Lambert}

